Spliced into the help2man-generated manual page by debian/rules.
help2man generates OPTIONS from --help; everything about configuring the
installed service lives here, so the options can never drift from the binary.

[DESCRIPTION]
.B agent-memory-mcp
is a shared long-term memory for coding agents. Claude Code, Codex and any
other Model Context Protocol (MCP) client can save memories and techniques,
and every other agent session can search and reuse them. The server speaks
MCP over Streamable HTTP at
.I /mcp
and stores entries in MongoDB.
.PP
There is no authentication. Restrict access at the network level, for
example with a firewall or Tailscale.
.PP
Every option can also be set with the environment variable shown next to it.
A command-line option overrides the environment.

[CONFIGURATION]
The packaged systemd unit,
.BR agent-memory-mcp.service ,
reads its settings from
.IR /etc/default/agent-memory-mcp ,
one
.I VARIABLE=value
per line. After editing it, run
.B systemctl restart agent-memory-mcp
and check the log with
.BR "journalctl -u agent-memory-mcp" .
.PP
At startup the server logs the Host names it accepts. Requests whose
.B Host
header is not on that list get HTTP 403 (DNS-rebinding protection), which MCP
clients usually report as a sign-in failure. Add every name and address
clients use in their server URL to
.BR ALLOWED_HOSTS .
Loopback names are always accepted.
.PP
The service runs as a transient
.B DynamicUser
in a locked-down sandbox and keeps no local state. All data lives in MongoDB,
in the database named by
.BR MONGODB_DATABASE ;
back that database up with
.BR mongodump (1).
.PP
To change the unit itself, use a drop-in rather than editing the packaged
file:
.B systemctl edit agent-memory-mcp
writes one to
.IR /etc/systemd/system/agent-memory-mcp.service.d/ .

[ENVIRONMENT]
.TP
.B MONGODB_URI
MongoDB connection string. Default
.IR mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017 .
.TP
.B MONGODB_DATABASE
Database to store memories in. Default
.IR agent_memory .
.TP
.B BIND_ADDR
Address and port to listen on. Default
.IR 0.0.0.0:8787 .
.TP
.B ALLOWED_HOSTS
Comma-separated extra Host names to accept, such as the machine's short
name, its Tailscale MagicDNS name and its tailnet IP.
.TP
.B ALLOW_ANY_HOST
Set to
.I true
to accept any Host header. Not recommended.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log level or filter:
.IR error ,
.IR warn ,
.IR info
(the packaged default),
.I debug
or
.IR trace .

[FILES]
.TP
.I /etc/default/agent-memory-mcp
Service configuration (a conffile; local edits survive upgrades). Mode 0600,
because a MongoDB connection string may carry credentials.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/agent-memory-mcp.service
The packaged systemd unit. Override it with a drop-in in
.IR /etc/systemd/system/agent-memory-mcp.service.d/ .
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/agent-memory-mcp
The server.

[EXAMPLES]
Accept clients that connect by short name, MagicDNS name or tailnet IP, in
.IR /etc/default/agent-memory-mcp :
.PP
.RS
.nf
ALLOWED_HOSTS=fuzzball,fuzzball.example-tailnet.ts.net,100.64.0.10
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run by hand against a remote MongoDB, listening only on loopback:
.PP
.RS
.nf
agent-memory-mcp --mongodb-uri mongodb://db.example:27017 --bind 127.0.0.1:8787
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check that the server is up:
.PP
.RS
.nf
curl http://localhost:8787/healthz
.fi
.RE

[SEE ALSO]
.BR systemd.exec (5),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR mongodump (1)
.PP
Project home and agent plugin setup:
.I https://github.com/opsnlops/agent-memory-mcp
